{"title":"Career Roadmap · AYUSH Medical Officer","role":"AYUSH Medical Officer","summary":"An AYUSH Medical Officer with a BUMS (Bachelor of Unani Medicine & Surgery) qualification provides healthcare within the scope of Unani medicine and applicable professional regulations, commonly through government AYUSH facilities, dispensaries, hospitals, wellness centres and public-health programs.","facts":{"Current degree":"BUMS (Unani)","Course":"Unani Medicine & Surgery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An AYUSH Medical Officer with a BUMS (Bachelor of Unani Medicine & Surgery) qualification provides healthcare within the scope of Unani medicine and applicable professional regulations, commonly through government AYUSH facilities, dispensaries, hospitals, wellness centres and public-health programs."},{"type":"h","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"h","text":"Unani clinical practice"},{"type":"h","text":"Preventive healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Unani pharmacology and therapeutics"},{"type":"h","text":"Community health"},{"type":"h","text":"Health education"},{"type":"h","text":"Public-health program implementation"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Referral and coordination"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact post title, eligibility, scope of practice, recruitment process and required registration can vary by government department and notification. A graduate must complete the recognised BUMS program, required internship and applicable registration requirements before practising independently."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"10+2 PCB"},{"type":"h","text":"NEET-UG"},{"type":"h","text":"Recognised BUMS"},{"type":"h","text":"Compulsory Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Registration"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH / Government Recruitment"},{"type":"h","text":